{"name":"Apple Wine","hex":"#b59f62","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apple wine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made from apples; cider."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple_wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apfelwein","blocks":[{"text":"Apfelwein, or Viez or Most are German words for cider. German ciders are made from various kinds of sour tasting apples and are distinguished by an alcohol content of 4.8–7.0% alongside a tart, sour taste."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Apfelwein_Geripptes_Bembel.jpg/330px-Apfelwein_Geripptes_Bembel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apfelwein"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org